WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:16.405
Sitting up in bed, I tried to calm myself.

2
00:00:17.465 --> 00:00:19.746
Maybe the sound I'd heard at my door was Pilot.

3
00:00:20.747 --> 00:00:25.288
Sometimes when the kitchen door was left open, the big dog found his way upstairs.

4
00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:30.010
In the mornings I'd often seen him lying in the corridor outside Mr.

5
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.051
Rochester's door.

6
00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.012
I lay down again and tried to sleep.

7
00:00:35.052 --> 00:00:39.453
But I'd barely closed my eyes when I heard a demonic laugh right next to me.

8
00:00:40.493 --> 00:00:44.855
The head of my bed was near the door, and at first I thought a goblin was crouching

9
00:00:44.895 --> 00:00:45.635
by my pillow.

10
00:00:46.695 --> 00:00:49.016
I rose, looked around, and saw nothing.

11
00:00:50.156 --> 00:00:55.858
Meanwhile the unnatural sound was repeated, and this time I knew it came from the other side of

12
00:00:55.898 --> 00:00:56.398
my door.

13
00:00:56.878 --> 00:01:01.839
My first impulse was to lock the door; my second was to cry out again, "Who's there?"

14
00:01:03.099 --> 00:01:04.820
Something gurgled and moaned.

15
00:01:05.888 --> 00:01:10.552
Before long I heard steps retreating down the corridor toward the third-story staircase.

16
00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:16.798
Then I heard the door at the foot of those stairs open and close, and all was still.

17
00:01:16.818 --> 00:01:18.920
"Was that Grace Poole?"

18
00:01:19.301 --> 00:01:20.081
I asked myself.

19
00:01:20.101 --> 00:01:22.584
"Is she possessed by a devil?

20
00:01:23.705 --> 00:01:25.106
I can't stay here by myself."

21
00:01:26.187 --> 00:01:30.171
I hurried to put on my dress and a shawl and opened my door to go in search

22
00:01:30.231 --> 00:01:30.571
of Mrs.

23
00:01:30.651 --> 00:01:35.855
Fairfax. Just outside the room, a burning candle sat on the floor.

24
00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:41.521
I was surprised by this, but I was even more amazed to find that the air was filled

25
00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:42.161
with smoke.

26
00:01:43.322 --> 00:01:45.304
I looked around and saw that Mr.

27
00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:46.966
Rochester's door was open.

28
00:01:48.087 --> 00:01:49.909
A cloud of smoke billowed out.

29
00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.191
I ran into the room.

30
00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:57.496
Tongues of flame darted around the bed, and the bed curtains were on fire!

31
00:01:58.696 --> 00:02:00.997
In the midst of the smoke and fire, Mr.

32
00:02:01.057 --> 00:02:03.358
Rochester lay motionless in a deep sleep.

33
00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:05.219
"Wake up!

34
00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:06.119
Wake up!"

35
00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:07.900
I screamed as I shook him.

36
00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:11.301
But the smoke had stupefied him.

37
00:02:12.302 --> 00:02:15.783
There wasn't a moment to lose because the sheets were catching fire.

38
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.564
I rushed to his basin and pitcher.

39
00:02:19.585 --> 00:02:24.046
Fortunately one was wide and the other was deep, and they were both filled with water.

40
00:02:25.107 --> 00:02:27.528
I threw the water on the bed and its occupant.

41
00:02:28.616 --> 00:02:33.998
Then I ran to my room for my own pitcher, hurried back, and poured the water over Mr.

42
00:02:34.058 --> 00:02:36.579
Rochester. "Is there a flood?"

43
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.400
he cried, waking at last.

44
00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.402
"No, sir, but there has been a fire," I replied.

45
00:02:42.422 --> 00:02:44.863
"Get up and I'll fetch you a candle."

46
00:02:44.883 --> 00:02:46.784
"Is that Jane Eyre?"

47
00:02:47.124 --> 00:02:47.784
he demanded.

48
00:02:47.804 --> 00:02:49.785
"What have you done to me?

49
00:02:50.786 --> 00:02:52.106
Were you plotting to drown me?"

50
00:02:52.126 --> 00:02:55.408
"Somebody has plotted something, sir!"

51
00:02:55.768 --> 00:02:56.108
I said.

52
00:02:57.928 --> 00:03:02.150
While he put on a dressing gown, I ran to fetch the candle from the corridor.

53
00:03:03.231 --> 00:03:09.334
He took it from my hand and surveyed the blackened bed, the drenched sheets, the soaked carpet.

54
00:03:10.355 --> 00:03:11.015
"What happened?

55
00:03:12.056 --> 00:03:12.696
Who did this?"

56
00:03:13.136 --> 00:03:13.717
he asked.

57
00:03:14.837 --> 00:03:19.440
I briefly told him what I had heard in my room and how I had extinguished the fire.

58
00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.642
He listened very gravely and did not immediately speak when I had concluded.

59
00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:26.663
"Shall I call Mrs.

60
00:03:26.704 --> 00:03:28.188
Fairfax?" I asked.

61
00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.009
"What can she do?

62
00:03:31.049 --> 00:03:32.349
Let her sleep undisturbed."

63
00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.930
"Then I will fetch Leah and wake John and his wife, Mary."

64
00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.811
"No, be still.

65
00:03:38.811 --> 00:03:43.012
Sit down in the armchair and place your feet on the stool to keep them dry," he said.

66
00:03:43.032 --> 00:03:44.733
"Are you cold?

67
00:03:45.753 --> 00:03:46.953
Let me help you with my cloak."

68
00:03:48.714 --> 00:03:51.815
He pulled out a long cloak and wrapped it around my shoulders.

69
00:03:51.835 --> 00:03:56.436
"I'm going to take the candle and leave you for a few minutes," he said.

70
00:03:57.504 --> 00:04:01.046
"Remain where you are until I return and be as quiet as a mouse.

71
00:04:02.286 --> 00:04:04.147
I must pay a visit to the third floor.

72
00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.989
Remember: don't move or call anyone."

73
00:04:09.089 --> 00:04:12.911
He left the room, and I heard him walk down the corridor very softly.

74
00:04:14.031 --> 00:04:18.993
Then he opened the staircase door with as little noise as possible and shut it after him.

75
00:04:20.014 --> 00:04:24.416
Left in total darkness, I listened for any noise but heard nothing.

76
00:04:25.512 --> 00:04:27.354
A very long time passed.

77
00:04:28.455 --> 00:04:31.458
I grew weary, and I was cold despite the cloak.

78
00:04:32.499 --> 00:04:36.442
I didn't see the point of staying and was on the verge of quietly returning to my room

79
00:04:36.823 --> 00:04:38.724
when I heard his footsteps in the corridor.

80
00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:42.208
Looking pale and very gloomy, Mr.

81
00:04:42.288 --> 00:04:43.709
Rochester entered the room.

82
00:04:43.729 --> 00:04:49.274
"It is as I thought," he said, setting the candle on the washstand.

83
00:04:49.294 --> 00:04:51.036
"What is, sir?"

84
00:04:52.052 --> 00:04:57.474
Mr. Rochester made no reply but stood with his arms folded, staring at the floor.

85
00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:03.676
After a few minutes he said in a rather peculiar tone, "I forget whether you said that you'd

86
00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.936
seen anything when you opened your bedroom door."

87
00:05:05.956 --> 00:05:08.757
"I only saw the candle on the floor."

88
00:05:08.777 --> 00:05:13.158
"But you've heard that laugh before or something like it?"

89
00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.779
"Yes, sir.

90
00:05:15.819 --> 00:05:18.280
There's a woman named Grace Poole who sews here.

91
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.682
She laughs in that way, and she's an odd person."

92
00:05:22.702 --> 00:05:26.605
"Just so Grace Poole you've guessed it.

93
00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:29.367
She is, as you say, odd.

94
00:05:30.528 --> 00:05:31.128
Very odd.

95
00:05:32.209 --> 00:05:34.170
Well, I shall think about this subject.

96
00:05:35.311 --> 00:05:39.414
Meanwhile I'm glad we're the only people who know the precise details of tonight's incident.

97
00:05:40.575 --> 00:05:41.575
Say nothing about it."

98
00:05:41.595 --> 00:05:43.757
"Yes, sir."

99
00:05:43.777 --> 00:05:48.200
"I'll account for this state of affairs," he said, pointing to the bed.

100
00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.070
"Now return to your own room.

101
00:05:52.231 --> 00:05:55.333
I shall do very well on the library sofa for the rest of the night.

102
00:05:56.434 --> 00:05:57.535
It's nearly four o'clock.

103
00:05:58.516 --> 00:06:00.077
In two hours the servants will be up."

104
00:06:01.138 --> 00:06:02.059
"Good night then, sir."

105
00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:03.980
I got up to leave.

106
00:06:05.081 --> 00:06:09.305
He looked surprised, which seemed odd to me as he'd just told me to go.

107
00:06:09.325 --> 00:06:11.867
"What!" he exclaimed.

108
00:06:11.887 --> 00:06:14.869
"Are you leaving me already and in that way?"

109
00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:17.612
"You said I might go, sir."

110
00:06:18.816 --> 00:06:23.379
"You've snatched me from a horrible and excruciating death, and you walk past me as if we were

111
00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:26.261
strangers! At least shake hands."

112
00:06:27.402 --> 00:06:29.603
He held out his hand and I gave him mine.

113
00:06:30.664 --> 00:06:34.086
He took it first in one and then in both his own hands.

114
00:06:34.106 --> 00:06:36.448
"You've saved my life.

115
00:06:37.669 --> 00:06:40.031
I have a pleasure in owing you so immense a debt."

116
00:06:41.812 --> 00:06:43.273
He paused and gazed at me.

117
00:06:44.494 --> 00:06:47.816
Words almost trembled on his lips, but he said nothing.

118
00:06:48.884 --> 00:06:50.005
"You owe me nothing, sir."

119
00:06:50.025 --> 00:06:54.066
"I knew you would do me good in some way when I first saw you.

120
00:06:55.127 --> 00:06:57.828
Your eyes did not strike delight in my heart for nothing.

121
00:06:58.908 --> 00:07:00.969
Good night, my cherished savior."

122
00:07:02.109 --> 00:07:06.451
Strange energy was in his voice, and strange fire was in his look.

123
00:07:06.471 --> 00:07:09.092
"I'm glad I happened to be awake.

124
00:07:10.153 --> 00:07:10.753
Good night, sir."

125
00:07:11.813 --> 00:07:13.914
I went back to bed but never thought of sleep.

126
00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:18.496
Too agitated to rest, I rose as soon as day dawned.
